# Spec for tools/riscpkg.py: FFmpeg.
Package: FFmpeg
Section: Video
Priority: Optional
Licence: Free
Maintainer: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Standards-Version: 0.4.0
Environment: arm32, vfpv3
Depends: SharedUnixLibrary (>= 1.16), ARMEABISupport
Components: Apps.Video.!FFmpeg (Movable LookAt)
Homepage: https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-ffmpeg
Description: FFmpeg 5.1 LTS (ffmpeg, ffprobe, ffplay) for ARMv7 NEON
 FFmpeg 5.1.10 with its NEON code, made safe for RISC OS's alignment
 checks: ffmpeg, ffprobe and ffplay, and an icon bar front end (drop a
 file on it to play or convert it). H.264 and HEVC hardware decoding
 on the Pi through ReelHWAccel. Needs ARMv7 with NEON.
Build-Map: !FFmpeg -> Apps/Video/!FFmpeg
Build-Untyped: auto fff
Build-Notice: FFmpeg, packaged for PackMan from the release zip on
 https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-ffmpeg/releases
 .
 FFmpeg 5.1.10 (ffmpeg.org) is built under the GNU GPL version 2 or
 later (it includes x264); the other libraries keep their own licences.
 The source is in the application's docs.source and on the release
 page. Licences follow.
Build-Copyright: !FFmpeg/docs/Licences
